From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH] spacemit: explicit suspend dispatch, genuine type-0 WFI, error propagation

First implementation batch of the OpenSBI/ESOS suspend-ownership plan
(OpenSBI owns the hart's architectural suspend/resume contract; ESOS
owns shared-resource eligibility). P0 items 1-3:

P0-1 EXPLICIT DISPATCH: __rpmi_hsm_suspend() previously routed every
type except 0x90000000 to the cluster power-down branch. Now:

- SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT (type 0): plain wfi() + return 0 —
  see P0-2
- SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_NON_RET_DEFAULT (0x80000000): REJECTED with
  SBI_ENOTSUPP (it previously took the cluster branch by accident;
  no qualified non-retentive default path exists)
- 0x90000000 (CPU non-retentive platform): per-CPU power-down vote,
  existing path unchanged
- K3_HSM_SUSP_CLUSTER_NON_RET (0x91000000): REJECTED with
  SBI_ENOTSUPP — cluster shutdown is NOT implemented until ESOS
  shared-domain ownership and the retained wake mechanism are
  qualified (plan P1; do not implement cluster shutdown as an
  automatic step)
- any other type: SBI_EINVAL — rejected BEFORE any hardware change:
  no vote, no cache/snoop/IMSIC operations

P0-2 GENUINE DEFAULT-RETENTIVE: type 0 returns before power votes,
interrupt masking, IMSIC manipulation, or cache changes. Register
state intact; caller resumes in place.

P0-3 ERROR PROPAGATION: the CONFIG_PLATFORM_SPACEMIT_K3 wrapper in
fdt_hsm_rpmi.c previously discarded __rpmi_hsm_suspend()'s result
and returned 0 unconditionally — rejected/failed suspends were
reported to the SBI caller as success. The result is now propagated,
with a one-line diagnostic (hart, type, error) on failure. Full
retained-counter/bounded-buffer diagnostics are follow-up work
(supporting deliverable).

Build-verified by disassembly (fw_dynamic.elf):
- type-0 path: exactly 'wfi; li a0,0; ret' at the beqz branch
- 0x80000000 compare -> li a0,-2 (SBI_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED) exit
- type-mask compare -> li a0,-3 (SBI_ERR_INVALID_PARAM) exit
- both rejection paths exit BEFORE any CSR write, vote call, or
  cache operation
- wrapper: bnez a0 -> sbi_printf failure path -> returns the
  backend's error code

HARDWARE QUALIFICATION REQUIRED (the acceptance criteria):
1. type 0 reaches WFI without side effects: no cluster vote, caches
   stay on, architectural state survives
2. non-retentive type 0x90000000 retains its behavior (regression)
3. wake from type-0: timer tick, IPI, UART — each wakes the hart
   and delivers
4. rejected types return their SBI error to the caller with no
   hardware change

Remaining P0 (follow-up batches, NOT in this patch): the non-
retentive context-preservation audit (P0-4), entry/abort/resume
cleanup ownership (P0-5), versioned capability discovery (P0-6).
ESOS-side P1 items (resource ownership, shared-domain state machine,
transactional votes, quiescence, retained wake, domain sequencing,
bounded transactions, clock ownership/rate policy) are prerequisites
for re-enabling cluster states.

--- a/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c
+++ b/lib/utils/hsm/fdt_hsm_rpmi.c
@@ static int rpmi_hsm_suspend(u32 type, ulong resume_addr)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_PLATFORM_SPACEMIT_K3
-	__rpmi_hsm_suspend(type);
+	int rc;
+
+	rc = __rpmi_hsm_suspend(type);
+	if (rc)
+		sbi_printf("rpmi-hsm: hart %u suspend type %#x failed: %d\n",
+			   current_hartid(), type, rc);
+	return rc;
 #else

--- a/platform/generic/spacemit/k3_corepm.c
+++ b/platform/generic/spacemit/k3_corepm.c
@@ int __rpmi_hsm_suspend(u32 type)
 {
+	/*
+	 * SBI HSM spec: SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT (type 0) is a plain
+	 * retentive wait-for-interrupt - no power management operations,
+	 * no votes, no cache/snoop changes; register state stays intact
+	 * and the caller resumes in place.
+	 */
+	if (type == SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_RET_DEFAULT) {
+		wfi();
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	[... existing IMSIC save / cache prep ...]
 
+	/*
+	 * EXPLICIT dispatch: only the supported non-retentive platform
+	 * type may vote power down. Unsupported types are rejected
+	 * BEFORE any hardware change.
+	 */
+	if (type == SBI_HSM_SUSPEND_NON_RET_DEFAULT)
+		return SBI_ENOTSUPP;
+
+	if (type != (SBI_HSM_SUSP_NON_RET_BIT | SBI_HSM_SUSP_PLAT_BASE) &&
+	    type != K3_HSM_SUSP_CLUSTER_NON_RET)
+		return SBI_EINVAL;
+
+	[... 0x90000000 keeps the per-CPU vote path ...]
+
+	} else {
+		/* cluster: UNSUPPORTED until ESOS ownership + retained
+		 * wake are qualified */
+		return SBI_ENOTSUPP;
+	}
